# A test run has opened `get` on Object.prototype. What a written descriptor leaves out is looked for above it: `{ value: v, enumerable: false }` finds the planted getter there, and Object.defineProperty() refuses the pair.
# So the literal is made and the built-in reads it. `{ get: g, configurable: true }` has the name itself, and none of the five that it leaves out is opened: it stays one operation. The question goes by the key.
# The records are those of the twin, definition-by-a-written-descriptor-is-one-operation.ir, where f1 is one DefineOwnProperty, and one more: the last line.
